The fix for #1059 works. I ran the built binary in an empty temp directory and in a fresh git init repository:

| Case | Output | Exit |
|---|---|---|
| yoyo undo --last-commit outside a repo | error: not in a git repository | 1 |
| yoyo undo --all outside a repo | error: not in a git repository | 1 |
| --last-commit in a repo with no commits | (no commits to undo) | 0 |
| --all in that repo (no uncommitted changes) | (nothing to undo — no uncommitted changes) | 0 |

• Intent: both --last-commit and --all now ask git whether this is a repository before reading anything, and stop with exit 1 if it isn't. All four git calls in --all now run in a given directory, so tests can use temp directories. The REPL /undo goes through the same code with the current directory, so it behaves as before.
• Leftover definitions: none. Each new function is called in the diff, there are no new enum variants, and the size limit for commands_git.rs was raised from 3722 to 3753 lines with a reason.
• Docs: the exit-code paragraph in docs/src/usage/commands.md now says both flags exit 1 outside a git repository.
• Product surface: this is a product task, and the only visible change is the exit status and message outside a repo, which matches diff, commit, blame and tree. No defaults or flags changed.
